le  recognizes so we have you know nine  sitemaps plus our main in the article  sitemap and a blog site map and if you  click in on either of these it'll show  you kind of a detailed list of every  page that we've indexed so we use a tool  that we'll talk about later to create  the site map but once you create the  site map you submit it to Google you  basically just  go here submit a sitemap and you add in  a URL so I'm Carl calm this would be  your website com / whatever and put your  site map in you should send XML type of  feed so that's why I see it here and  what's really beneficial is you can see  if there's any problems with your  sitemap so here there's there's been a  problem with the sitemaps we have 11  pages submitted 9 our index and there's  some issue so we need to look at that  and see what see what's going on if we  look at our main articles we can see we  have almost 60,000 that have been  contributed to the site map and almost  all of them are indexed so it shows that  the content is being picked up and is  being indexed by Google what you can do  if you don't have as much content i  don't expect most people to have you  know a hundred thousand pages of content  on their site what it can do is show you  which pages are being indexed and which  ones aren't which is really important so  if you know that you're submitting pages  to google and they're not recognizing  those pages are not in the index maybe  there's something wrong with those pages  that you can fix up and resubmit so that  they will be indexed these other site  maps are other files that we have on the  side that could have pictures into them  or forum posts or other things that they  may not always get picked up so we don't  really care too much about these ones  but I pay a lot of attention to this you  know if only half of articles are being  indexed and that would be a major  problem then we'd have to look at how we  can fix those up so that's that's what's  useful about the sitemaps it helps the  search engines know which articles are  on your site and it helps you figure out  which articles are being indexed in  which ones aren't and if there's any  problems they'll let you know so that's  a great way to do it now to create a  site map it can be super easy you don't  need to have a lot of technical  experience to do it so what I use if I  go to my favorite tools here this is a  page i use to showcase all the tools  that are used to run my business i use a  free tool free is always a magic word  for business owners it's called g site  crawler Angie site crawler is a free  download that it's a as a pc software  you download onto your computer you put  in your URL and basically what it will  do is crawl your website like Google so  they'll start on your homepage and then  start going to all the sub pages and  then  create a site map for you so to create  that site map it has to be in a specific  language that the search engines  understand and if you're not a very  technical person it can be a little  overwhelming to try to create that so  what we'll do is use G site crawler will  do this once a month for for our site  because we have a lot of ongoing stuff  that's happening with our business if  you don't have a lot of changes and you  don't need to do it as frequently but  this program does too cool thing is one  it creates a sitemap and will  automatically you know generate that  file which all you have to do is upload  to your website and then go back to  google and click submit a sitemap and  put in the URL the other really cool  thing about it is it will tell you if  there's any errors with your website so  let's hope there's any crawl errors so  you might be linking to a page it  doesn't exist anymore because you've  updated it or you change your template  or you're trying to pull in a picture  that doesn't exist it tells you what  those errors are and gives you a big  list it tells you where the arrows are  generated from and what you need to do  to fix it so that's great to either do  yourself or give to your technical guy  to be able to go in and make those site  changes because the more those kind of  broken links you have or broken images  somewhere on your website the more of  those you have the worst looks or Google  and you could potentially have a penalty  hit on your site usually those types of  errors are not on your homepage you're  very deep on some old page that you  haven't updated for years but if you  have enough of them that could look bad  in the search engines eyes so you  definitely want to fix those up and  again g sy crawler does that for you and  it's completely free so Stan I hope that  helps answer your question if you guys  liked the video please give the video a  thumbs up below i always appreciate  seeing those you know those thumbs ups  coming in and if you have any comments  so if you're using a different program  i'd love to hear from you if you want to  leave a comment under the video and I'll  always do my best to respond to you or  maybe even make a video reply so thank  you and we'll see you on the next  episode  I  you
 

